  "model": "gpt-5.6-terra",
  "reasoning_effort": "high",
  "prompt": "prompts/physics_committee_terra_round2_v1.md",
  "preferred_configuration": {
    "prize_parts": [
      {
        "ballot_id": "B014",
        "laureates": [
          "Hidetoshi Katori",
          "Jun Ye"
        ],
        "citation": "for the conception and experimental realization of optical lattice clocks"
      }
    ]
  },
  "alternatives": [
    "B032",
    "B018"
  ],
  "statement": {
    "case_for": "I have changed my preferred configuration from B032 to B014. The magic-wavelength lattice-clock principle is a particularly clean solution to the conflict between trapping many atoms and preserving clock accuracy. Its development has produced a reproducible platform with quantified systematic control and demonstrated reach to precision measurements of time, gravity, and fundamental physics. This joins an essential physical mechanism to a mature realization unusually well. Katori and Ye provide a suitably compact attribution when the achievement is defined narrowly as the lattice-clock concept and its decisive realization.",
    "case_against": "The optical-clock field is wider than this two-person account: the citation must not imply credit for all optical-frequency metrology, its infrastructure, or a future standards redefinition. My previous preference, B032, remains a deep and durable theoretical framework, but it comprises closely related relations and a later framework rather than one comparably bounded discovery-to-realization chain. Its experimental validation is meaningful, yet less decisive for present priority than the mature, independently realized B014 platform.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "member_id": "johansson-goran",
        "point": "Johansson held that fluctuation relations are elegant and mature but asked for a stronger account of how the related theorems form one bounded prize achievement, contrasting this with the experimentally singular lattice-clock realization.",
        "response": "I accept this distinction. Jarzynski, Crooks, and Seifert describe a coherent intellectual development, but the need to delimit equality, relation, and framework remains material. B014 has the more sharply specified physical problem, solution, and experimentally settled realization, which changes my comparative judgment without diminishing B032's importance."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "danielsson-ulf",
        "point": "Danielsson argued that B014 combines a sharply defined magic-wavelength idea, repeatedly demonstrated experimental control, and a bounded Katori-Ye attribution, provided the award is not extended to the entire optical-clock enterprise.",
        "response": "I agree with that boundary. It is precisely the narrow link between the physical principle and its defining realization that makes B014 stronger than a generic award for optical clocks. The demonstrated systematic control and independent realization supply the maturity that I previously weighed more heavily in favor of a general theoretical framework."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "lindroth-eva",
        "point": "Lindroth emphasized that the lattice clock preserves high signal from many atoms while suppressing trapping-induced frequency shifts, and warned that a future redefinition of the second should not be treated as an accomplished outcome.",
        "response": "This is the right physical and evidential framing. The prize need not rely on a prospective metrological decision: the established precision platform and its demonstrated measurement capabilities already make the case. The citation should retain the lattice-clock boundary so that the two credited names do not stand in for the whole optical-clock lineage."
      }
    ],
    "uncertainties": [
      "Historical review must still establish whether Katori and Ye alone adequately represent the foundational magic-wavelength lattice-clock concept and decisive realization.",
      "The final citation must distinguish the lattice-clock achievement from the broader optical-clock and metrology enterprise.",
      "For B032, the exact boundary among the Jarzynski equality, Crooks relation, and stochastic-thermodynamic framework remains relevant if it is reconsidered in a later year."
    ],
    "conflict_note": "No conflict requiring recusal is apparent. I share the Gothenburg physics environment with Göran Johansson and Eva Olsson, but no specific collaboration is identified in the supplied profile."
  }
}
